Data licence — data/bsep_chembl.parquet
=======================================

This file applies ONLY to the bundled dataset at `data/bsep_chembl.parquet`
and its derived fixture at `data/example/bsep_example.parquet`. The source
code and the trained weights in `src/vp_bsep/` are licensed separately under
Apache-2.0; see LICENSE.

Source
------
ChEMBL (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/), target CHEMBL6020 — bile salt export
pump, Homo sapiens, UniProt O95342. Activity records of standard_type IC50 and
Ki, retrieved 2026-06-04 via the ChEMBL activity REST API.

Derivation
----------
Nanomolar potencies were converted to micromolar; a ">" standard_relation was
treated as a censored inactive; structures were standardised (normalise,
largest fragment, neutralise) and collapsed to one row per InChIKey by median
potency; the binary label applies a 100 µM cutoff to that median. Only the
InChIKey, standardised SMILES, binary label, median potency and measurement
count are retained.

